nt to help  me finish this and he said yeah and  that's how the song came back so I that  so that's the single shine a light of  this album and I expected a duo between  you two on the album why didn't I was an  IDI not on the album I don't know it was  just it was it's what it's the way it is  you know and you know one of the things  I love that you just said that artists  when they make music they're in a place  in their lives in their career and that  influences our music and you were just  talking about your dad how would you  describe the journey of this album well  one of the things about the way I work  is I sort of sort of assemble ideas and  harcum I collaborate mostly I work with  a guy called Jim Vallance and I've  worked with for many years and we just  spend the last couple years I've been  working on a musical with him in New  York and so while we were working on the  musical I was just working on other  ideas and trying to put together this  album so it's it was a lot of a lot of  writing it's like for that for musical  alone we wrote over 30 songs and and for  the album there's another 12 so maybe 4  to 15 so the songs always keep coming  you know it doesn't necessarily mean  they're gonna do anything but music  keeps happening are you consistently  writing every day not every day but  ideas happen all the time yeah another  collaboration you did was genuine the  blog Jennifer Lopez I mean how did that  happen did you guys get in the studio  together did you give her a call or it  was just a concept that came up the the  song that's on the album with Jennifer  Lopez is coach that's how strong our  love  and I'd actually recorded the song mixed  it finished it and then I've done you  know what I'd like to sing this with  somebody I think I'd like to find some  and and and I thought of Jennifer I  thought I'd be interesting too I'd met  her many many years ago in in Spain and  I thought so I wrote an email to her  manager I said do you think Jennifer  